markdown <<MARKDOWN
# Education Specific Tools

LLMs are powerful, general-purpose tools that can generate text, summarize information, and respond to a wide range of prompts. While they are useful for many tasks, they are not always the best fit for classroom use.

In response, developers have created education-specific AI tools—applications built on similar technology but designed for school settings. These tools are often more focused and aligned to educator needs, often providing a safer and more structured way to integrate AI into teaching and learning.

Education-specific AI tools may include features such as:
* Built-in guardrails that limit inappropriate or unsafe use
* Stronger privacy protections aligned to school requirements
* Interfaces and outputs designed specifically for educator tasks

When exploring these tools, look for ones that:
* Prioritize student privacy
* Provide teacher controls or visibility
* Support learning and thinking—not just answer-giving

While these tools can be helpful, they still require thoughtful use.

<br>

<div style="text-align: center; width: 80%; margin: 0 auto;">
  <p style="
    font-size: 18px; 
    background-color: #F5F7F8; 
    padding: 10px; 
    border-left: 5px solid #8148B2; 
    border-right: 5px solid #8148B2;
    display: inline-block;
  "><strong>Important Disclaimer</strong> <br><br>Just because a tool was designed specifically for educational use does not mean it's okay to use in your school or classroom. <br><br><strong>When in doubt always follow school and district guidelines.</strong>
  </p>
</div>

